[00:35.82]And American skier Lindsey Vonn cut her hand badly while she was opening a glass bottle to celebrate winning at the 2009 World Championships.
[00:47.20]We know you’re not professionals, but we want you to tell us all about your silliest sporting accidents.
[00:56.40]Last year, I was playing volleyball for my school team.
[01:00.68]I jumped up high and hit the ball really hard.
[01:04.10]At first, I thought it was a really good shot, but I soon found out it wasn’t.
[01:10.16]The ball hit the post at the side of the net: then it hit me in the face and knocked me to the floor.
[01:17.00]I had a big purple bruise on my face and I couldn’t play the rest of the game.
[01:24.30]When I was 13, I played for the school rugby team and we won the schools championship.
[01:31.32]A few days later, there was a big celebration.
[01:35.68]All the students were there to watch as we walked on to the stage to get medals from the headmistress.
[01:42.60]I got my medal, but when I was leaving the stage, I tripped and fell down the steps.
[01:49.66]Luckily, I wasn’t hurt, but I was really, really embarrassed.
